// The act break (bible 7.1 step 6; character-bibles.md §1). The Road That Stops (Road_3). Wren steps off the road's
// end into the white without a tether and stays herself: Clarity. Pell, sent by Voss to watch her, sees.
// Pell's lists shorten as they grow surer: five things here, three in Halden, one at the Return.

title: Edge_Pell_Watch
---
<<if not has_flag("isolde.cache")>>
    Road: The road stops mid-stride, a step from the white.
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
<<if has_flag("pell.saw_her_cross")>>
    Pell: I wrote it down. All five. I haven't sent it. Which, technically, isn't the same as not sending it.
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Road: The road ends mid-stride. She steps off it, into the white, without a tether.
Road: Thirty steps. A hundred. The white leans on her, and she stays herself.
<<grant Clarity>>
Road: She comes back. Somebody is standing at the road's end, holding a notebook.
Pell: Five things. One, you walked in without a tether. Two, you were gone eleven minutes.
Pell: Three, you kept your colour. Four, so did I, watching, which I didn't expect.
Pell: Five. You came back.
Pell: Wren. How?
-> I don't know. It knew me.
    Pell: That's not an answer. It's the most frightening thing anyone's said to me. #plant:5.3
    <<voice drift greyfold>>
-> Isolde measured it. Her pages.
    Pell: Her pages. Which, technically, you're meant to surrender. I'll write that you didn't.
    <<voice surveyor greyfold>>
-> Pell. Don't write this down.
    Pell: I have to. Voss sent me to watch you. I'm the one who'd get it right.
    <<voice warden greyfold>>
Pell: The Guild says you're missing. You're not missing. You're the least missing person I know.
<<flag pell.saw_her_cross 1>>
<<flag act2.started 1>>
===
